Generated Media Frontier =E2=80=94 2 strong finds

   1. Avatar-Forever =E2=80=94 Ruibin Li et al. =E2=80=94 TEST NOW ON GPU
   GitHub: https://github.com/leeruibin/avatarforever
   Paper: https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.12107

Material delta: inference code is now publicly available. The system
separates few-step generation from long-horizon robustness: a distilled 22B
generator handles efficiency, while a lightweight Recovery-oriented Rollout
Training adapter learns to recover from accumulated autoregressive errors.
ForeverCache reuses historical features across denoising steps. The paper
reports effectively unbounded audio-driven 768x512 generation at 27.2 FPS
on one H100. Code is runnable in a Python 3.11/CUDA environment;
weights/code availability should be checked in the repo before committing
compute. Maturity: RUNNABLE / research-grade.

Why it matters: this is directly relevant to persistent hosts. Most avatar
systems optimize short clips; Avatar-Forever explicitly trains against
long-horizon drift. Exact experiment: run a 10=E2=80=9330 minute continuous
monologue with a fixed identity and quantify face-embedding drift,
background drift, A/V sync and recovery after deliberately bad history
chunks. Compare against our current long-form avatar candidate. If stable,
this is a candidate premium continuous renderer; its Recovery-oriented
Rollout Training idea is also worth borrowing independently.

   1. voqalize/avatar =E2=80=94 Voqalize =E2=80=94 ADOPT/MINE NOW
   GitHub: https://github.com/voqalize/avatar

A new MIT Pipecat-focused avatar library with a surprisingly good
embodiment protocol. It does not send a video track or charge per-minute
rendering. The backend infers SPEAKING/LISTENING/THINKING/WORKING states
from ordinary Pipecat frames, sends three wire commands
(claim/action/cues), and the browser renders SVG/Canvas2D avatars locally.
Its lip-sync is especially clever: a ~0.15 ms text-predicted viseme path
starts immediately, then an audio recognizer overwrites it as PCM arrives;
if accurate decoding falls behind real time, it permanently falls back
rather than applying late corrections. The native wheel is ~44 MB. MIT
licensed; Linux x86-64/aarch64 and macOS arm64 lipsync wheels. Maturity:
RUNNABLE / integration-grade.

Why it matters: this is the cleanest implementation I=E2=80=99ve found yet =
of the
Performance IR/control-contract idea. We should not copy its art; we should
copy/test its wire semantics: durable state + point actions + timestamped
viseme cues, with renderer independence. Exact experiment: put our Jev-like
acting policy upstream and emit claim/action/cues into a custom renderer.
This could become the low-cost draft/runtime contract while photoreal
renderers remain replaceable.

TOP 5 TO TEST RIGHT NOW

   1. Avatar-Forever 10=E2=80=9330 minute identity-drift torture test.
   2. Voqalize wire protocol as our Performance IR prototype.
   3. Jev-like policy -> Voqalize action/state commands.
   4. Swap Voqalize=E2=80=99s Canvas/SVG renderer for a VRM/Three.js render=
er
   without changing controller semantics.
   5. Preserve the same Performance IR and replay selected performances
   through a premium diffusion renderer.

BEST OPEN-SOURCE AI INFLUENCER STACK THIS HOUR
persona/memory -> creative LLM -> cheap Jev-like policy -> Performance IR
(state/action/viseme timeline) -> browser VRM/Canvas draft -> multimodal
critic -> Avatar-Forever/premium video renderer for selected outputs ->
Remotion/FFmpeg -> publish -> engagement feedback.

BIGGEST CAPABILITY JUMP
Avatar-Forever=E2=80=99s released inference path: long-horizon robustness i=
s
becoming a first-class trainable component rather than hoping a short-video
diffusion model stays coherent indefinitely.

CHEAPEST PRACTICAL WIN
Voqalize=E2=80=99s tiny renderer-independent state/action/cue protocol. It =
gives us
an implementable Performance IR immediately with local rendering and no
video transport.

WATCH NEXT

   - leeruibin/avatarforever
   - voqalize/avatar
   - GAIR/interactive-avatar-style long-horizon streaming work

STACK DELTA
Formalize Performance IR now. Use three semantic classes modeled after the
strongest Voqalize idea: durable STATE, finite ACTION, timed
SPEECH/PERFORMANCE CUES. Keep identity/persona/audience history above this
layer and renderer adapters below it. Add a long-horizon drift benchmark to
renderer qualification. Do not change the rest of the stack this hour.

Suppressed repeats: talk2avatar, threejs-talking-avatar, InfiniteTalk and
generic MuseTalk wrappers had no verified material delta worth repeating in
this scan.

